 "critic": "Most cards felt assembled because names were precise while motives, possessions, crews, and jobs stayed generic. Three-option menus often joined different needs without explaining their connection, and final sentences about reputation or being a stranger felt detachable. Pronoun shifts exposed joins. Repeated collector messages and exact duplicates reinforced that impression after rating. Injury disrupting income and protection money creating a deadline supplied convincing consequences even when the wording felt generated. Surveillance and gang-expulsion requests lacked underlying motives. Ivo's refusal, threatened escalation, and organizing stalls formed the most convincing local chain of events."
